==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|fi|orv|}} (compare {{cog|ru|воробей}}); nativized with the diminutive {{m|fi|-nen}} suffix.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[sparrow]]
#* {{quote-song|fi|year=1913|author={{w|Zacharius Topelius}} (original poem in Swedish, 1859), {{w|K. A. Waaranen|lang=fi}} (Finnish translation, 1880s), {{w|Otto Kotilainen|lang=fi}} (composer)|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Sparven om julmorgonen|Varpunen jouluaamuna}}|trans-title=A Sparrow on Christmas Morning|url=https://fi.wikisource.org/wiki/Varpunen_jouluaamuna|text=Lumi on jo peittänyt kukat laaksosessa,<br/>järven aalto jäätynyt talvipakkasessa.<br/>'''Varpunen''' pienoinen, syönyt kesäeinehen,<br/>järven aalto jäätynyt talvipakkasessa.|translation=Snow has fallen, through it pokes not a single heather,<br/>waves of water turned to ice by the wintry weather.<br/>A '''sparrow''' so little with nothing to eat and live,<br/>waves of water turned to ice by the wintry weather.|lit=The snow has already covered the flowers in the dale,<br/>the waves of the lake have been frozen by the cold winter weather.<br/>A tiny '''sparrow''' has eaten the (last of its) summer food,<br/>the waves of the lake have been frozen by the cold winter weather.}}
# {{lb|fi|as modifier in compound terms}} [[passerine]], [[sparrow]]
#: {{usex|fi|'''varpus'''lintu|'''passerine''' bird|inline=1}}
